        <mxCell id="9S01YbboC7UPRPZFMBvF-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1&gt;Clean Architecture&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;In clean architecture, the control and dependency flow move inward toward the business logic. All outward-facing components (such as data access, external services, and the UI) depend on the inner layers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;Furthermore, the business logic is separated into single-responsibility use cases.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
